Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Run each MIDI subscriber in its own try/catch

MidiHub raised its events with a plain `?.Invoke`, which stops at the first
handler that throws :

 - the handlers registered after it never get the message ;
 - ProcessQueue is left mid-queue (the rest waits for the next tick) ;
 - EditorApplication.update skips its remaining callbacks for the frame.

OnCC has three subscribers in this project (KontrolsWindow.OnMidiCC,
KontrolsWindow.OnTempoCC, Presets' PresetRecall.OnCc). One that throws on
every message -- a binding to a destroyed object, a scene-dependent target
after a scene switch -- leaves every later subscriber dead while the port is
perfectly alive : the same symptom as a lost controller, without one.

Each subscriber of OnCC, OnNote, OnPitchBend, OnRealtime, OnConnectionChanged
and of the learn callbacks now runs in its own try/catch (Each<T>, over
GetInvocationList). A failing handler is logged with its declaring type and
method, once per 5 s per handler, not once per message : a turning knob sends
dozens a second and a flooded console slows the editor down.

Cost : one invocation-list array and one closure per dispatched message,
negligible at MIDI rates.

Applies on top of patch 2 (OnConnectionChanged is raised from its watchdog).
